0c0602b14e300c6ed5fa97eb2410cca57fbab517a4ffdc7b8c19fa40a33.png)\n\nJohn, a meteorologist, took $16$ temperature measurements in Melbourne. The results are presented above in the form of a histogram. Find an estimate of the mean temperature.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."}] :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Mean From Grouped Data" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049397 :topic/math-academy-id 126 :topic/title "Estimating Means and Variances For Grouped Data"}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054679 :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055176 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052362}] :question/math-academy-id "q-253145" :question/problem "Consider the frequency table below, where $x$ is continuous, and the total number of observations is $n = 30$.\n\n| Range | Frequency ($f_{i}$) |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $-2 \\le x < 0$ | $8$ |\n| $0 \\le x < 2$ | $9$ |\n| $2 \\le x < 4$ | $8$ |\n| $4 \\le x < 10$ | $5$ |\n\nGiven that an estimate for the mean is $x^(―) \\approx 2$, find an estimate for the variance $σ_{n}^{2}$.\n\nRounded to the **nearest integer**, $σ_{n}^{2} \\approx$\n{{field-1}}\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055177 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052363}] :question/math-academy-id "q-253146" :question/problem "The call center manager of a small taxi service wants to estimate the standard deviation of the times between taxi requests. The following frequency table reports the times, in minutes, recorded on a particular day.\n\n| Observations ($x_{i}$) | Frequency ($f_{i}$) |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $0 \\le x < 20$ | $8$ |\n| $20 \\le x < 40$ | $10$ |\n| $40 \\le x < 60$ | $7$ |\n\nGiven that an estimate of the sample mean is $x^(―) \\approx 29.